Overlay patch 0056 (D24, port of Shipwright 0066 / D-085): SPIKE
ATTRIBUTION PROBE (GS_SPIKE / GS_SPKWIN).

WHY. 0055's GS_PACE can say THAT the game thread was busy in a frame, not
WITH WHAT. On Shipwright this probe found the per-tick depth readback and the
touch overlay's full-screen repaint inside the SDL pump; Ghostship shares the
shell and the LUS seams, so it ships the same instrument (default ON) and
the user's OTA session produces the phone numbers.

WHAT IT MEASURES. Every 2D engine frame is cut at the 0055 pace seams
(drawable acquired / LUS sleep begins) plus three marks inside
Fast3dWindow::DrawAndRunGraphicsCommands; the record closes right after
Interpreter::EndFrame (post-sleep):

  gap    previous frame's post-sleep -> this frame's drawable request. Holds
         the game tick on the first frame of each tick (logic), the audio
         hand-off wait (aud), SDL_PumpEvents = every UIKit main-thread
         callback (ev), FrameInterpolation_Interpolate (interp).
  wait   nextDrawable (0055).
  busy   drawable -> LUS sleep (0055), split into
           menu  ImGui NewFrame + DrawMenu + CalculateGameViewport (0057 splits it)
           run   Interpreter::StartFrame + Run (the display list)
           gui   Gui::EndDraw (DrawGame, ImGui render)
           end   Metal EndFrame (commit, present) up to the sleep
  logic  previous tick's audio-wait exit -> RunCommands entry (the SM64 tick:
         thread5_iteration's game logic + display-list build)
  cpu    gap + busy. A frame whose cpu exceeds the frame period
         (1000 / interpolation fps: 8.33 ms at 120) is a SPIKE.

Seam categories (game thread = the main thread on iOS, pthread_main_np):
   0 res    resource cache MISS loaded on the game thread (n / ms / bytes,
            3 largest by name)
   1 rd     the archive read part of res
   2 bg     cache misses loaded on the resource pool threads
   3 rwait  ResourceManager::LoadResource on the game thread (hits + waits)
   4 tex    Interpreter::ImportTexture (decode + upload of a new texture)
   5 up     Interpreter::UploadBaseTexture (n / bytes; ms is inside tex)
   6 shd    CreateAndLoadNewShader on the game thread
   7 fbrd   ReadFramebufferToCPU (GPU wait)
   8 cvsave ConsoleVariables::Save (CVarSave and the Gui's deferred save)
   9 aud    EndAudioFrame waiting on the audio thread
  10 ev     wnd->HandleEvents (SDL pump: touches, timers, the 0.25 s poll)
  11 interp FrameInterpolation_Interpolate
plus per-frame triangles / vertices / draw calls. SoH's zdep/zpso (depth
readback), actor/obj/room seams are not ported: SM64 never calls
GetPixelDepth (D25) and has no equivalent spawn seams worth a hook.

OUTPUT.
  GS_SPIKE   one line per spike frame, at most 20 per 10 s window.
  GS_SPKWIN  one line per 10 s: frames, spikes, cpu p50/p95/max, per-frame
             average of each split over ALL frames / over SPIKE frames, each
             category's n / total ms / ms inside spike frames (+MB), content
             counters.

COST. Two mach_absolute_time reads and a pthread_main_np per seam event, a
handful of steady_clock reads per frame, no allocation in the hot path.
gSohIos.SpikeProbe (default 1) switches it off (re-read every 60 frames).

Generate against a vendor tree with 0001..0055 applied and 0056 not applied.


